{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1019986-the-otodo-from-dark-eras","id":1019986,"title":"The Otodo from Dark Eras","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-20T14:49:30-08:00","id":1019986,"title":"The Otodo from Dark Eras","content":"First off, this is my first post for Hunter: the Vigil. I love H:tV! I'm picking up Compacts and Conspiracies this weekend, and I can't wait <br /> for 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> That said, my theory is that although the Otodo think their patriarch is a demon, he is actually an Oni, a unique Ogre kith native to Japan. I was inspired to hypothesize this by the fact that in D&amp;D, the Oni (ogre magi) are actually a subspecies of ogre. My theory is supported by the fact that the Otodo feel a special kinship with the Lost, referring to them as &quot;cousins.&quot; What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T17:38:21-08:00","id":1020076,"title":"","content":"Presumably, they're just as much related to the demons from <i>Inferno</i> as the main European Lucifuge are, but canon is a joke and do whatever works at your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T22:30:57-08:00","id":1020188,"title":"","content":"I believe we already have a kith called Oni in the kith spoilers. I think their blessing was that they could spot out 'outsiders' in a given group, and conjure minor storms, the former being related to Asian group-oriented culture and the latter more directly related to what Oni are associated with in legends.<br /> <br /> Of course, as atamajakki says, the sole purpose of canon is to provide base materials for you to work with. Maybe the founder of the Otodo line was a legendary changeling of the Ogre seeming. Or maybe the founder was indeed a faerie ogre on the mortal world... but not a mere changeling, but a True Fae.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}